===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:strete|tree=1}}

{{inh+|en|enm|strete}}, from {{inh|en|ang-ang|strēt||street|ng=compare {{cog|ang-wsx|strǣt}}}} from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*strātu|t=street}}, an early {{lg|borrowing}} from {{der|en|la-lat|([[via]]) [[strāta]]|t=paved (road)}}, from {{der|en|la|strātus}}, past participle of {{m|la|sternō||stretch out, spread, bestrew with, cover, pave}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sterh₃-||to stretch out, extend, spread}}. {{dbt|en|estrade|stratum}}.

The {{IPAchar|/aː/}} vowel of the Latin etymon shifted by {{w|Anglo-Frisian brightening}} to {{IPAchar|/æː/}} in West Saxon and {{IPAchar|/eː/}} in Anglian Old English; these developed respectively to {{IPAchar|/ɛː/}} and {{IPAchar|/eː/}} in Middle English, {{IPAchar|/ɛː/}} and {{IPAchar|/iː/}}  in Early Modern English, and finally {{IPAchar|/iː/}} in Modern English by the {{w|Great Vowel Shift}}. The modern spelling reflects the Anglian form, as in {{m|en|sleep}}, {{m|en|greedy}}, {{m|en|sheep}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
